    "updated_at": "2022-02-21T20:59:55Z",
    "body": "> do you have any ideas on which symbol to use?\r\n\r\nSo this is Spack's logo: \r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155024749-f24a4187-353f-4aeb-8e84-22e68e419e15.png)\r\n\r\n\r\nQuickly glancing through Nerd Fonts, a few ideas:\r\n\r\n- `f7a1` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025104-c0966211-188f-4cf1-9aac-ca180de22688.png) gets the closest, but it's just git's logo, so basically already taken.\r\n- `f009` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155024823-c9075c77-9fee-43c5-bf08-cfb5c372d351.png) (boxes meaning packages), \r\n\r\n- `e225` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155024918-74aece9b-9c1a-4f39-9242-f8d0f60b7424.png) or `f63a` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155024967-89493b34-8abe-490d-a3c2-580fba1b2e95.png) is kinda close to spack's logo \r\n- `fc09` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025236-a4eeb352-baa0-4c98-96c4-c42a5412d776.png) or `fc0a` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025271-8f6f5181-b400-4d16-978d-84346b1b1158.png) would be the outline of Spack's logo\r\n- `f9a9` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025370-eedde39b-c331-4aa0-94ac-7be09dfbee01.png),  `fa5f` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025453-60d73412-9a3c-4a44-a8bf-4ffcdec04ea4.png), and `f493` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025490-f054bd3e-7e28-44ab-97be-21bff09006a1.png) has the branching stuff similar to spack's logo\r\n\r\nAlternatively, we could use `e27d` ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/20801821/155025623-62267f3b-2cd6-4e73-99ca-c245a5d148ab.png), which is apparently a magazine logo, but I've literally never heard of it before. I think this would be the best, assuming it's not already taken.",
